  "body": "## Result and scope\n\nAlgebraic component only; **no new supplier or \u03ba**. Adds `research/norm6-dyadic-decoder/` without changing the selected construction.\n\nFor the 26,208,000 minimum-vector lines of an extremal 48-dimensional even unimodular lattice, this proves:\n\n- a norm-one binary chart in dimension 49, with the correct forbidden-pair identity;\n- the fitting kernel `((x\u00b7y)^3\u22124(x\u00b7y))/192`;\n- an explicit 19,648-term dyadic factorization and an algebraic support-rank bill at most 962,752.\n\nMinimum six and the full shell cardinality remain published dependencies from Nebe / the Nebe\u2013Sloane P48p catalogue. The package checks the exact Gram and positive LDL factorization; it does not enumerate the full shell. The missing side program, bit rail, physical copying, hosting and precision remain explicit open obligations.\n\n## Verification\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/norm6-dyadic-decoder\n```\n\nPassed locally on Python 3.12 / NumPy 1.26.4 / SymPy 1.12, including the registered optimized entry point: full symbolic coefficient comparison, binary chart, 676 sampled pairings and three mathematical mutations. Normal verification writes nothing. Hosted CI is separate and is not claimed green here.\n\n## Prior work and review\n\nThe incorporated Leech/PR598 and Niemeier investigations retain credit for polynomial-lattice kernels, dyadic integer features and the lattice direction. The addition is the explicit minimum-six construction and 49-bit chart, not a claim to originate polynomial kernels. `OVERLAP.md` records the complete open-PR metadata screen (453 initially, refreshed to 457), detailed related submissions, discussion coverage and limits. No matching norm-six/P48 package appeared in that screen; this is not a universal novelty guarantee.\n\nPrepared by Cinna Davis (@1337isnot1337) with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0; original mathematical/data attribution retained. No independent human review or full multiplication theorem formalization is claimed.\n",
